course: dictionary
lesson: 4668
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one to use. Hold is a good example. «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant» means keep it in your hand. «A pack holds 3 cards» means a pack has room for 3 cards. The words around hold are the clues.
explain: Look at «Horses can sleep standing up because a locking system in their legs, the stay apparatus, holds them up.» Here hold means keep something up and in place. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
explain: Hold can also be a noun, meaning a grip. «Hold the rail» and «hold hands when you cross» are safety rules, and a hold is the grip you have on something. The same word can be a doing word in one sentence and a naming word in another.
fact: Hold can mean to grip something, to have room for something, or to keep something in a certain place or state.
fact: «Hold» can also mean to have or organise an event, such as a party or a meeting.
fact: «Hold on» in everyday talk means wait a moment.
fact: «A pack holds 3 cards»: if one pack holds 3 cards, then 4 packs hold 12 cards, so multiply to find the total.
fact: A hold is a grip, as when you get a firm hold on a rope.
exercise: «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge.» In this sentence, what does hold mean? | Have a party | *Keep it in your hand | Be empty | Wait a moment
exercise: «A pack holds 3 cards.» You have 4 packs. How many cards do the packs hold in total? | 7 | 3 | 34 | *12
exercise: Grandad says, «Hold on a minute!» What does hold on mean? | Put it down and leave | *Wait a moment | Start a race | Climb a tree
test: «Horses can sleep standing up because the stay apparatus holds them up.» What does holds mean here? | Lets them fall down | Makes them run fast | Has a party for them | *Keeps them up, in place
test: Mia needs 24 sweets for a party. Each bag holds 6 sweets. How many bags does she need? | 6 | 30 | 18 | *4
exam: In which sentence does hold mean a grip? | *The climber found a good hold on the rock | We hold a meeting every Monday | The bottle holds one litre of water | Please hold on, I am coming
